===

INT. SPACE STATION - COMMAND CENTER - NIGHT

The command center hums with the sound of computers and life support systems. Warning lights flash across multiple monitors.

COMMANDER SARAH CHEN (40s, determined, exhausted) stands at the main console, her reflection ghosted in the darkened viewport showing the void beyond.

[[Note: This opening establishes the isolation and tension]]

SARAH
Houston, this is ISS-7. We've lost contact with the supply ship. Again.

She waits. Static fills the silence.

SARAH (CONT'D)
(whispering to herself)
Come on... not again.

The door hisses open. DR. JAMES MARTINEZ (50s, calm under pressure) enters carrying a tablet.

MARTINEZ
Sarah, you need to see this.

He crosses to her station, placing the tablet on the console. Data streams across the screen - unusual energy readings.

SARAH
What am I looking at?

MARTINEZ
The signal we've been tracking. It's not random interference. It's a pattern.

SARAH
(leaning closer)
A pattern? From where?

===

EXT. SPACE STATION - VIEWPORT - NIGHT

Through the station's massive viewport, stars shimmer against the infinite black. A subtle pulse of light appears in the distance, barely visible.

===

INT. SPACE STATION - COMMAND CENTER - NIGHT

Sarah and Martinez stare at the readings, the implications dawning on them.

MARTINEZ
It's coming from the dark side of the moon.

SARAH
That's impossible. There's nothing there.

MARTINEZ
Exactly. There shouldn't be anything there.

The computer beeps. New data appears on screen.

SARAH
(reading)
The signal's getting stronger. It's like... it's like it's trying to reach us.

She looks up at Martinez, fear and wonder mixing in her expression.

MARTINEZ
We need to tell Houston.

SARAH
They won't believe us. Hell, I don't believe us.

===

INT. SPACE STATION - LABORATORY - DAY

The lab is cluttered with equipment and floating tablets. YUKI TANAKA (30s, brilliant, skeptical) analyzes data at a workstation while eating from a pouch of rehydrated food.

Martinez enters, pulling himself through the zero-gravity environment.

YUKI
Let me guess. You want me to confirm your alien signal theory?

MARTINEZ
(smiling)
Would you?

YUKI
(turning to face him)
James, I've analyzed every wavelength. It's electromagnetic radiation with a repeating sequence. That doesn't make it extraterrestrial.

MARTINEZ
But you can't explain the source.

Yuki pauses, considering.

YUKI
No. I can't.

MARTINEZ
Then help us figure out what it is.

===

INT. SPACE STATION - SARAH'S QUARTERS - NIGHT

A small, personal space. Photos of Earth, family pictures magnetically attached to the walls. Sarah floats near her sleeping bag, a tablet in hand showing the signal pattern.

Her fingers trace the data, searching for meaning in the chaos.

SARAH
(to herself)
What are you trying to tell us?

A notification appears on her tablet. Message from Houston.

She opens it, reading quickly. Her expression darkens.

SARAH (CONT'D)
No... they can't order us to ignore this.

===

EXT. MOON - DARK SIDE - DAY

The lunar surface, stark and ancient. In a crater, barely visible against the regolith, something glints in the harsh sunlight.

A structure. Not natural. Not human.

===

INT. SPACE STATION - COMMAND CENTER - DAY

The full crew assembled: Sarah, Martinez, Yuki, and PILOT ALEX PETROV (30s, impulsive, brave).

SARAH
Houston wants us to maintain our current mission parameters and ignore the signal.

ALEX
(in Russian accent)
Ignore it? Are they serious?

YUKI
It could be a natural phenomenon. We don't know enough to—

ALEX
Or it could be the most important discovery in human history!

MARTINEZ
Sarah, you're the commander. What do we do?

The weight of the decision settles on Sarah's shoulders. She looks at each crew member, then at the data on the screens.

SARAH
We investigate. Prep the lunar lander.

ALEX
(grinning)
Now we're talking!

YUKI
This is a mistake.

SARAH
Maybe. But it's my mistake to make.

CUT TO:

INT. LUNAR LANDER - DAY

Cramped. Technical. Sarah and Alex run through pre-flight checks while Yuki and Martinez monitor from the station.

MARTINEZ (V.O.)
(over radio)
Lander One, you are go for separation.

SARAH
Copy that. Initiating release sequence.

A series of mechanical clicks and hisses.

ALEX
Here we go.

===

EXT. SPACE - LUNAR LANDER - DAY

The small craft separates from the station, firing thrusters to begin its descent toward the moon.

===

INT. LUNAR LANDER - CONTINUOUS

Sarah pilots while Alex monitors the signal strength.

ALEX
Signal's getting stronger. We're definitely headed in the right direction.

SARAH
ETA to landing site, three minutes.

Through the window, the lunar surface grows closer, the ancient crater coming into view.

ALEX
Sarah... look.

In the crater, the structure is now clearly visible. Geometric. Deliberate. Alien.

SARAH
(breathless)
Houston... you need to see this.

FADE TO BLACK.
